 margin-bottom: 10px; font-weight: bold;'><span class='question-badge'>15</span> 15. What's the common quality of leaders?</p><input type='hidden' id='ans-15' value=''><div class='option-group' data-question='15'><div class='option-item' data-value='A'><span class='option-radio'></span><span class='option-text'><strong>A</strong> Have good public speaking skills.</span></div><div class='option-item' data-value='B'><span class='option-radio'></span><span class='option-text'><strong>B</strong> Solve all problems skillfully.</span></div><div class='option-item' data-value='C'><span class='option-radio'></span><span class='option-text'><strong>C</strong> Be respected by the workforce.</span></div></div></div><div style='background: #ffffff; border: 1px solid #e4e7eb; padding: 20px; border-radius: 10px;'><p style='margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 10px; font-weight: bold;'><span class='question-badge'>16</span> 16. How should companies take risks?</p><input type='hidden' id='ans-16' value=''><div class='option-group' data-question='16'><div class='option-item' data-value='A'><span class='option-radio'></span><span class='option-text'><strong>A</strong> Deal with them carefully.</span></div><div class='option-item' data-value='B'><span class='option-radio'></span><span class='option-text'><strong>B</strong> Be financially advantageous.</span></div><div class='option-item' data-value='C'><span class='option-radio'></span><span class='option-text'><strong>C</strong> Think in the long run.</span></div></div></div></div><div style='background-color: #f1f2f6; border-left: 5px solid #00cec9; padding: 15px; border-radius: 8px; margin-top: 25px; margin-bottom: 20px;'><strong style='display: block; font-size: 1.05rem; margin-bottom: 5px;'>Questions 17 and 18</strong><span style='font-size: 0.9rem; color: #57606f;'>Choose <strong>TWO</strong> letters, <strong>A–E</strong>. Which TWO factors are important when starting a business?</span></div><div style='background: #ffffff; border: 1px solid #e4e7eb; padding: 25px; border-radius: 10px; margin-bottom: 25px; line-height: 1.8;'><div style='background: #f8f9fa; border: 1px solid #e1e8ed; padding: 15px 20px; border-radius: 8px; margin-bottom: 15px; display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: 8px; font-weight: 500;'><div><strong>A</strong> Fix realistic prices.</div><div><strong>B</strong> Create products better than the competitors'.</div><div><strong>C</strong> Be committed.</div><div><strong>D</strong> Pay attention to detail.</div><div><strong>E</strong> Apply complete strategy.</div></div><div style='display: flex; gap: 20px; align-items: center; flex-wrap: wrap;'><span>Lựa chọn thứ nhất: <span class='question-badge'>17</span> <input type='text' id='ans-17' style='width: 60px; padding: 6px; text-align: center; font-weight: bold; text-transform: uppercase; border: 1px solid #ced6e0; border-radius: 6px; outline: none;'></span><span>Lựa chọn thứ hai: <span class='question-badge'>18</span> <input type='text' id='ans-18' style='width: 60px; padding: 6px; text-align: center; font-weight: bold; text-transform: uppercase; border: 1px solid #ced6e0; border-radius: 6px; outline: none;'></span></div></div><div style='background-color: #f1f2f6; border-left: 5px solid #00cec9; padding: 15px; border-radius: 8px; margin-top: 25px; margin-bottom: 20px;'><strong style='display: block; font-size: 1.05rem; margin-bottom: 5px;'>Questions 19 and 20</strong><span style='font-size: 0.9rem; color: #57606f;'>Choose <strong>TWO</strong> letters, <strong>A–E</strong>. Which TWO kinds of support are important for Arthur?</span></div><div style='background: #ffffff; border: 1px solid #e4e7eb; padding: 25px; border-radius: 10px; margin-bottom: 25px; line-height: 1.8;'><div style='background: #f8f9fa; border: 1px solid #e1e8ed; padding: 15px 20px; border-radius: 8px; margin-bottom: 15px; display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: 8px; font-weight: 500;'><div><strong>A</strong> Family support.</div><div><strong>B</strong> Good business advice with new ideas.</div><div><strong>C</strong> Support of the bank loan.</div><div><strong>D</strong> Friends' support.</div><div><strong>E</strong> Governmental funding.</div></div><div style='display: flex; gap: 20px; align-items: center; flex-wrap: wrap;'><span>Lựa chọn thứ nhất: <span class='question-badge'>19</span> <input type='text' id='ans-19' style='width: 60px; padding: 6px; text-align: center; font-weight: bold; text-transform: uppercase; border: 1px solid #ced6e0; border-radius: 6px; outline: none;'></span><span>Lựa chọn thứ hai: <span class='question-badge'>20</span> <input type='text' id='ans-20' style='width: 60px; padding: 6px; text-align: center; font-weight: bold; text-transform: uppercase; border: 1px solid #ced6e0; border-radius: 6px; outline: none;'></span></div></div>",
        "q3": "<div style='background-color: #f1f2f6; border-left: 5px solid #fab1a0; padding: 15px; border-radius: 8px; margin-bottom: 20px;'><strong style='display: block; font-size: 1.05rem; margin-bottom: 5px;'>Part 3: Questions 21-30</strong><span style='font-size: 0.9rem; color: #57606f;'>Questions 21-24: Choose the correct letter, <strong>A, B or C</strong>.</span></div><h3 style='color: #2f3542; text-align: center; font-size: 1.4rem; margin-bottom: 20px;'>DOLPHIN PRESENTATION</h3><div style='display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 16px; margin-bottom: 30px;'><div style='background: #ffffff; border: 1px solid #e4e7eb; padding: 20px; border-radius: 10px;'><p style='margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 10px; font-weight: bold;'><span class='question-badge'>21</span> 21. What is the students’ purpose in mentioning the way dolphins make sounds?</p><input type='hidden' id='ans-21' value=''><div class='option-group' data-question='21'><div class='option-item' data-value='A'><span class='option-radio'></span><span class='option-text'><strong>A</strong> To show comparison with human speech.</span></div><div class='option-item' data-value='B'><span class='option-radio'></span><span class='option-text'><strong>B</strong> To show the unusual anatomy of a dolphin's head.</span></div><div class='option-item' data-value='C'><span class='option-radio'></span><span class='option-text'><strong>C</strong> To show recent developments in understanding the meaning of the sounds.</span></div></div></div><div style='background: #ffffff; border: 1px solid #e4e7eb; padding: 20px; border-radius: 10px;'><p style='margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 10px; font-weight: bold;'><span class='question-badge'>22</span> 22. According to Fran, Hector’s dolphins are unaffected by</p><input type='hidden' id='ans-22' value=''><div class='option-group' data-question='22'><div class='option-item' data-value='A'><span class='option-radio'></span><span class='option-text'><strong>A</strong> tourist numbers.</span></div><div class='option-item' data-value='B'><span class='option-radio'></span><span class='option-text'><strong>B</strong> the threat from fishing nets.</span></div><div class='option-item' data-value='C'><span class='option-radio'></span><span class='option-text'><strong>C</strong> their slow breeding rate.</span></div></div></div><div style='background: #ffffff; border: 1px solid #e4e7eb; padding: 20px; border-radius: 10px;'><p style='margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 10px; font-weight: bold;'><span class='question-badge'>23</span> 23. The New Zealand Government set up a marine sanctuary</p><input type='hidden' id='ans-23' value=''><div class='option-group' data-question='23'><div class='option-item' data-value='A'><span class='option-radio'></span><span class='option-text'><strong>A</strong> because of public pressure.</span></div><div class='option-item' data-value='B'><span class='option-radio'></span><span class='option-text'><strong>B</strong> as a result of scientific research.</span></div><div class='option-item' data-value='C'><span class='option-radio'></span><span class='option-text'><strong>C</strong> to protect a dolphin feeding ground.</span></div></div></div><div style='background: #ffffff; border: 1px solid #e4e7eb; padding: 20px; border-radius: 10px;'><p style='margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 10px; font-weight: bold;'><span class='question-badge'>24</span> 24. Where is the largest population of Hector’s dolphins in New Zealand?</p><input type='hidden' id='ans-24' value=''><div class='option-group' data-question='24'><div class='option-item' data-value='A'><span class='option-radio'></span><span class='option-text'><strong>A</strong> The east coast.</span></div><div class='option-item' data-value='B'><span class='option-radio'></span><span class='option-text'><strong>B</strong> Southland.</span></div><div class='option-item' data-value='C'><span class='option-radio'></span><span class='option-text'><strong>C</strong> The west coast.</span></div></div></div></div><div style='background-color: #f1f2f6; border-left: 5px solid #fab1a0; padding: 15px; border-radius: 8px; margin-top: 25px; margin-bottom: 20px;'><strong style='display: block; font-size: 1.05rem; margin-bottom: 5px;'>Questions 25-30</strong><span style='font-size: 0.9rem; color: #57606f;'>Write the correct letter, <strong>A–H</strong>, next to questions 25-30. Which special characteristic does each of the following types of dolphin have?</span></div><div style='background: #ffffff; border: 1px solid #e4e7eb; padding: 25px; border-radius: 10px; line-height: 1.8;'><div style='background: #f8f9fa; border: 1px solid #e1e8ed; padding: 20px; border-radius: 8px; margin-bottom: 20px;'><h4 style='margin-top: 0; border-bottom: 1px solid #e1e8ed; padding-bottom: 8px; color: #e67e22; text-align: center;'>Special characteristics</h4><div style='display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: 8px; font-weight: 500;'><div><strong>A</strong> Swim along behind boats.</div><div><strong>B</strong> Swim in unusually large groups.</div><div><strong>C</strong> Live along New Zealand's entire coastline.</div><div><strong>D</strong> Swim beneath slow-moving boats.</div><div><strong>E</strong> Tend to be solitary.</div><div><strong>F</strong> Live only off New Zealand's northwest coast.</div><div><strong>G</strong> Are the second largest dolphin species in New Zealand.</div><div><strong>H</strong> Are seen mostly in Kaikoura.</div></div></div><h4 style='color: #2f3542; margin-top: 15px; margin-bottom: 15px;'>Types of dolphin</h4><div style='display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 15px;'><div>• 25. Common dolphins: <span class='question-badge'>25</span> <input type='text' id='ans-25' style='width: 60px; padding: 6px; text-align: center; font-weight: bold; text-transform: uppercase; border: 1px solid #ced6e0; border-radius: 6px; outline: none;'></div><div>• 26. Dusky dolphins: <span class='question-badge'>26</span> <input type='text' id='ans-26' style='width: 60px; padding: 6px; text-align: center; font-weight: bold; text-transform: uppercase; border: 1px solid #ced6e0; border-radius: 6px; outline: none;'></div><div>• 27. Hector's dolphins: <span class='question-badge'>27</span> <input type='text' id='ans-27' style='width: 60px; padding: 6px; text-align: center; font-weight: bold; text-transform: uppercase; border: 1px solid #ced6e0; border-radius: 6px; outline: none;'></div><div>• 28. Maui's dolphins: <span class='question-badge'>28</span> <input type='text' id='ans-28' style='width: 60px; padding: 6px; text-align: center; font-weight: bold; text-transform: uppercase; border: 1px solid #ced6e0; border-radius: 6px; outline: none;'></div><div>• 29. Orcas: <span class='question-badge'>29</span> <input type='text' id='ans-29' style='width: 60px; padding: 6px; text-align: center; font-weight: bold; text-transform: uppercase; border: 1px solid #ced6e0; border-radius: 6px; outline: none;'></div><div>• 30. Bottle-nose dolphins: <span class='question-badge'>30</span> <input type='text' id='ans-30' style='width: 60px; padding: 6px; text-align: center; font-weight: bold; text-transform: uppercase; border: 1px solid #ced6e0; border-radius: 6px; outline: none;'></div></div></div>",
        "q4": "<div style='background-color: #f1f2f6; border-left: 5px solid #e84393; padding: 15px; border-radius: 8px; margin-bottom: 20px;'><strong style='display: block; font-size: 1.05rem; margin-bottom: 5px;'>Part 4: Questions 31-40</strong><span style='font-size: 0.9rem; color: #57606f;'>Questions 31-34: Complete the notes below. Write <strong>ONE WORD ONLY</strong> for each answer.</span></div><div style='background: #fdfefe; border: 1px solid #e4e7eb; padding: 25px; border-radius: 10px; margin-bottom: 25px; line-height: 1.8;'><h2 style='margin-top: 0; color: #e84393; border-bottom: 2px solid #f1f2f6; padding-bottom: 10px; text-align: center;'>RECYCLING TYRES IN AUSTRALIA</h2><h3 style='color: #2f3542; margin-top: 20px; border-left: 4px solid #e84393; padding-left: 10px;'>Background</h3><ul style='list-style-type: none; padding-left: 5px;'><li style='margin-bottom: 12px;'>• More than 1.5 million tyres dumped in Australia per <span class='question-badge'>31</span> <input type='text' id='ans-31' style='width: 180px; padding: 6px; border: 1px solid #ced6e0; border-radius: 6px; outline: none;'></li><li style='margin-bottom: 12px;'>• Previous recycling attempts failed because:</li><li style='margin-left: 20px; margin-bottom: 8px;'>– there were pollution problems – smoke from burning</li><li style='margin-left: 20px; margin-bottom: 12px;'>– recycling companies didn’t make any <span class='question-badge'>32</span> <input type='text' id='ans-32' style='width: 180px; padding: 6px; border: 1px solid #ced6e0; border-radius: 6px; outline: none;'></li></ul><h3 style='color: #2f3542; margin-top: 20px; border-left: 4px solid #e84393; padding-left: 10px;'>Advantages of Molectra’s process</h3><ul style='list-style-type: none; padding-left: 5px;'><li style='margin-bottom: 12px;'>• More economical because smaller machines are used</li><li style='margin-bottom: 12px;'>• Less maintenance – tyres softened before shredding</li><li style='margin-bottom: 12px;'>• No limit on the <span class='question-badge'>33</span> <input type='text' id='ans-33' style='width: 180px; padding: 6px; border: 1px solid #ced6e0; border-radius: 6px; outline: none;'> of tyres recycled</li></ul><h3 style='color: #2f3542; margin-top: 20px; border-left: 4px solid #e84393; padding-left: 10px;'>The Future</h3><ul style='list-style-type: none; padding-left: 5px;'><li style='margin-bottom: 12px;'>• Ten more factories being built</li><li style='margin-bottom: 12px;'>• Plans to spend 5% of income each year on <span class='question-badge'>34</span> <input type='text' id='ans-34' style='width: 180px; padding: 6px; border: 1px solid #ced6e0; border-radius: 6px; outline: none;'></li></ul></div><div style='background-color: #f1f2f6; border-left: 5px solid #e84393; padding: 15px; border-radius: 8px; margin-bottom: 20px;'><strong style='display: block; font-size: 1.05rem; margin-bottom: 5px;'>Questions 35-40</strong><span style='font-size: 0.9rem; color: #57606f;'>Complete the flow-chart below. Write <strong>ONE WORD ONLY</strong> for each answer.</span></div><div style='background: #ffffff; border: 1px solid #e4e7eb; padding: 25px; border-radius: 10px; line-height: 1.8;'><h3 style='margin-top: 0; color: #e84393; border-bottom: 2px solid #f1f2f6; padding-bottom: 8px; text-align: center;'>RECYCLING TYRES - Process</h3><div style='display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 15px; margin-top: 20px;'><div style='background: #fdfefe; border: 1px solid #ced6e0; padding: 15px; border-radius: 8px;'>Removal of steel <span class='question-badge'>35</span> <input type='text' id='ans-35' style='width: 160px; padding: 6px; border: 1px solid #ced6e0; border-radius: 6px; outline: none;'> from tyre rim<br><span style='color: #57606f;'>➔ Steel pellets used in industry</span></div><div style='text-align: center; color: #747d8c; font-weight: bold; font-size: 1.2rem; margin: -5px 0;'>↓</div><div style='background: #fdfefe; border: 1px solid #ced6e0; padding: 15px; border-radius: 8px;'>Chemicals applied to get rid of <span class='question-badge'>36</span> <input type='text' id='ans-36' style='width: 160px; padding: 6px; border: 1px solid #ced6e0; border-radius: 6px; outline: none;'> and soften rubber</div><div style='text-align: center; color: #747d8c; font-weight: bold; font-size: 1.2rem; margin: -5px 0;'>↓</div><div style='background: #fdfefe; border: 1px solid #ced6e0; padding: 15px; border-radius: 8px;'>Fibres, e.g. nylon, removed<br><span style='color: #57606f;'>➔ Strengthening concrete</span><br><span style='color: #57606f;'>➔ Sheets made of <span class='question-badge'>37</span> <input type='text' id='ans-37' style='width: 160px; padding: 6px; border: 1px solid #ced6e0; border-radius: 6px; outline: none;'></span></div><div style='text-align: center; color: #747d8c; font-weight: bold; font-size: 1.2rem; margin: -5px 0;'>↓</div><div style='background: #fdfefe; border: 1px solid #ced6e0; padding: 15px; border-radius: 8px;'>Tyres cut up into crumb rubber<br><span style='color: #57606f;'>➔ Asphalt for roads</span><br><span style='color: #57606f;'>➔ Insulation</span><br><span style='color: #57606f;'>➔ <span class='question-badge'>38</span> <input type='text' id='ans-38' style='width: 160px; padding: 6px; border: 1px solid #ced6e0; border-radius: 6px; outline: none;'> tiles</span></div><div style='text-align: center; color: #747d8c; font-weight: bold; font-size: 1.2rem; margin: -5px 0;'>↓</div><div style='background: #fdfefe; border: 1px solid #ced6e0; padding: 15px; border-radius: 8px;'>The MolectraVac machine microwaves rubber into hydrocarbon<br><br><strong>i) Used for activated carbon:</strong><br><span style='padding-left: 15px;'>• <span class='question-badge'>39</span> <input type='text' id='ans-39' style='width: 160px; padding: 6px; border: 1px solid #ced6e0; border-radius: 6px; outline: none;'> treatment</span><br><span style='padding-left: 15px;'>• air filtration</span><br><br><strong>ii) Used for carbon black:</strong><br><span style='padding-left: 15px;'>• batteries</span><br><span style='padding-left: 15px;'>• <span class='question-badge'>40</span> <input type='text' id='ans-40' style='width: 160px; padding: 6px; border: 1px solid #ced6e0; border-radius: 6px; outline: none;'></span><br><br><strong>iii) Oil used for electricity</strong></div></div></div>"
